The remote embedding for a service that truncates at tokens: texts whole, a timeout of
30 s, no retry of a refused request, the local model loaded only when needed

What: with EMBED_API_KEY and EMBED_API_URL set, add_embeddings_to_source sends each
text whole (max_chars=None) instead of its first 1,000 characters; a 400 that says
`context length` then fails at once instead of halving a cap. _embed waits 30 s instead
of 120 s, and any 4xx but 429 fails at once instead of being retried 4 times; network
errors, timeouts, 429 and 5xx are retried as before. Every failure falls back to local
embedding, as before. TransformResources loads the local model lazily (lazy_load=True):
the session starts on the first local embedding, so a batch the service embeds does not
load it.

Why: the modama search stack embeds the warehouse's texts on grace's GPU through a
service of its own (prototypes/search-stack/embedding-service/), which tokenizes and
truncates at the model's 512 tokens as the local path does; cut at 1,000 characters
(about 200 to 250 tokens), every longer record would get another vector than locally. A
wrong token or another model fails the same way four times and cost 7 s of backoff per
batch; the search API's client retries only network errors, timeouts, 429 and 5xx too.
In requests the timeout limits the connection and each wait for bytes, so a hanging
service now costs about 2 minutes per batch before the fallback, not 8. Without
lazy_load, each batch process loaded the model whether or not it embedded locally.

Same result for the local path: unchanged; lazy_load only moves the load to the first
embed call (fastembed 0.8.0, `_embed_documents`: load_onnx_model when the session is
missing), with the same threads.

Against metadata-warehouse v1.10.0 with 0001 to 0004 applied; applied with `patch -p1`
in the image build (modama search stack, warehouse-airflow.Dockerfile; change
embedding-service-grace, D2, Q7, Q8). Written against 0001 to 0003; its first hunk was
regenerated when 0004 (change embedding-fp32-model) landed, which shapes the same
TextEmbedding call: `lazy_load=True,` is now a line after 0004's
`specific_model_path=model_path,`. The hunks of embedding_utils.py are unchanged.

